ame. It's his biggest scam yet. Donald Trump announced he would be launching his own social media network named Truth Social. The fact about Truth Social is a vehicle for standing up for the tyranny of BitTech, which conservatives claim hate free speech, prohibits users to say anything, disparage the site. Guess what? You can't say anything bad about Trump on the site. Meanwhile, a whole thing is built on a crappy aversion in Twitter. You can use truths, which are like tweets or retweets, which are retweets. And Trump is doing this in a SPAC, which is a kind of a reverse engineering thing where people put money into it, but he has no money into it. He can only win. Everybody else can only lose. Guess what? It's a merger, a new company, the Trump and Media and Technology Group, another scam for Trump. Trump's social media called Truth, a brand down for Trump. Big brain down for Biden in the polls, the latest polls on Biden are really kind of very sobering for Democrats. His latest approval voting in his CNBC approval rating is 41% and 52% disapprove. That's an 11-point net rating compared with a positive three points in the July survey. We're 48% approved and 48% approved and 45% disapproved. That's a 14-point swing. He's going from 3 up to 11 down. That's in July. That's in a few months. And that's a combination of things. It started with Afghanistan, of course. Obviously, the Delta variant has not helped. Him not be able to get his bills passed is not helped. And I think his overall, the feeling that he projects, he just doesn't seem to be projecting dynamism and strength. Of course, that was never, he's at a certain age where that was never gonna be a strength, but he just doesn't seem to have his hands firmly on the wheel. People are becoming really concerned about the economy. The number one thing that people are not concerned about rightfully so is inflation. It's up 16 points from the previous survey. People are concerned about a recession. So, economy started