 for the third workplace and Sax is somebody that, that I kind of Don't believe in this, but it's happening. So we'll give it a brand up. I think it's stupid so I can give it a brand down. It's something called the Third Workplace. The pandemic is given rise to something called the Third Workplace, where there are places that work that aren't one us at home or office. It's a WeWork situation for a membership of $300 a month or $50 a day. You can join SACS works. SACS, Fifth Avenue, working with WeWork, where people who don't want to work at home, But they don't not ready to go back to the office. So they're afraid of going back, but they don't have to go back to the office. And it's like you get upscale perks, such as hydroponic gardens and gyms equipped with peloton bikes. I think this is nonsense. I think if people think there's not enough options that working at home or working at work, and now you get these other kind of weird, I just think we're coddling workers too much. And I know that. corporate america as a challenge now a lot of people don't want to go back to work and people have in trouble finding labor but i don't know i just think we're coddling our workers too much in this third workplace just give me a break okay face broke brand down for fate will brand question mark their rebranding themselves face book is going to be announcing a company named next week to reflect its focus on building the metaverse so what they want to set up is that basically Facebook is going to be or what we perceive to be Facebook with a corporation of Facebook is bigger than social media because obviously, you know, social media is kind of charged with a lot of negativity these days. Obviously, there's a lot of their business. They already have a lot of their, they want to rebrand to show that they're overseeing groups like Instagram, WhatsApp, Oculus, and more. They're doing a lot obviously with A.I. and VR. They're creating something called Horizon. The name is still unrel