    "turn_text": "I'm sure, you know, about six months before the election, I spoke to the speaker and suggested that we form a room group of members to try to anticipate all the things that go wrong in the election. And what if the Electoral College was tied with the Vice President didn't count electors from a particular state? We basically gained now. She thought it was a good idea. So we gained now a little group of us. All the 1,000 things that might happen except the one that did, a bleeding insurrection. And the morning of the insurrection, I was on the House floor, I was there for the whole time, because I was charged to having come up with this idea of being one of the managers to oppose Republican efforts to de-certified results. And I really wasn't paying attention to what was going on outside the building. I was too busy focused on what I was going to say with the Republicans were arguing how would I would rebut what they were saying. And the first thing that I knew something was wrong, I looked up and the speaker was no longer interchair presiding. And I knew that she had fully planned to preside for the entire joint session.",
